Third-party software this code depends on (installed separately, not included in this repository):
- doc_reader (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/Taeksu-Kim/doc_reader) — the `doc_parser.a2a` A2A endpoint.
- stt (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/Taeksu-Kim/stt) — optional, transcribes videos without human-made subtitles (called over A2A).
- FastAPI, Starlette, Uvicorn, httpx (MIT / BSD) — the server.
- FFmpeg (LGPL-2.1+ / GPL depending on the build) — called as an external program.
- yt-dlp (Unlicense) — called as an external program for video addresses.
- Summarizers (one or both): a local LLM served by vLLM (Apache-2.0) with an OpenAI-compatible API, or the Claude Code CLI.
- Optional: pytest (MIT), Playwright (Apache-2.0), Pillow (MIT-CMU) for tests, the browser check and screenshots.

Screenshots and example outputs in docs/ show frames and summaries of publicly available YouTube videos
(TED "Inside the Mind of a Master Procrastinator" — CC BY-NC-ND 4.0; 까칠한AI; 길벗 IT 전문서) for documentation only.
Their uploader subtitle files are not included.
